    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "For most homeowners in Utah, the average cost of a full roof replacement ranges from $8,500 to $19,500 for a standard home using asphalt shingles. A typical 2,000-square-foot home generally averages around $11,000 to $15,000 for a full tear-off and new installation .",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "$8,500 to $19,500"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The final invoice changes based on the size of your home, location, and the materials you choose."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Average Cost by Home Size"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Because roofing materials are priced per \"square\" (a 100-square-foot patch), the overall footprint of your home is the largest cost driver."
